From 113f970dcb93381d8aba79bf3707d3310d188906 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joe Poyzer <poyzerj@live.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 19:12:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Canvas notes: add_lab_text/delete_lab_text, and IPv6 in IP
 labels

New add_lab_text tool puts free text on the lab canvas (VLAN and group
names, notes such as "D2 is acting as a L2 switch", titles), beside a
node (below/above/left/right) or at exact pixels, with colour,
background, font size and bold options. It is nudged off existing
text. delete_lab_text removes notes by ID or all at once. Notes are
kept by clear_lab_labels and label_lab_ips reruns, and label_lab_ips
now places its labels around them. Text is HTML-escaped and colours
are restricted to plain colour values.

label_lab_ips now shows global IPv6 addresses next to ports and under
SVIs/loopbacks (link-local skipped), and reads VPCS IPv6 from
`show ipv6`.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TrazMEvGjE9pveiknF3Abo
